    {
      "post_id": "580325090367315968",
      "text": "Flight #4U9525 initially climbed to 38,000 feet before before it started to descend and lost signal at 6,800 feet. http://t.co/MthXQ232Hn",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:07:38 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": null,
      "post_type": "source"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "581194453471260672",
      "text": "@marcepa49 the flight profile. That doesn't indicate that the autopilot was set to 100 feet. I've worked on these systems, tested them",
      "timestamp": "Thu Mar 26 20:42:10 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.810756606905754e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "581063618730553344",
      "text": "@Minus777 @flightradar24 @isobelroe That's what they say.",
      "timestamp": "Thu Mar 26 12:02:17 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.810623463211909e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "581065934598582272",
      "text": "@marcepa49 @flightradar24 @isobelroe It only takes a moment to enter 7700 into the transponder. I've worked on these systems before.",
      "timestamp": "Thu Mar 26 12:11:29 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.8106463637359e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "581065199672655873",
      "text": "@marcepa49 @flightradar24 @isobelroe distress call. I thought it was hi-jacked and being flown by then. If it's true that the co-pilot did",
      "timestamp": "Thu Mar 26 12:08:33 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.8106463637359e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580330009153286144",
      "text": "@marcepa49 @neilh1983 @london_thfc @flightradar24 @isobelroe The mountains aren't real high there.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:27:10 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803299325779804e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580477423487180800",
      "text": "@marcepa49 @flightradar24 @isobelroe Anyway. Have to wait and see now.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 21:12:57 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.804769023449416e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580330462729670656",
      "text": "@Minus777 @london_thfc @flightradar24 @isobelroe In case of a deliberate crash it would have descended faster, no?",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:28:58 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803292117447639e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "581065340110655488",
      "text": "@marcepa49 @flightradar24 @isobelroe crash it deliberately, the whole industry needs a shake-up.",
      "timestamp": "Thu Mar 26 12:09:07 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.8106463637359e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580325250996518913",
      "text": "@flightradar24 any idea why it'd flight so high?  It's a short flight, usually planes go at ~ 33,000 feet",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:08:16 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.80325090367316e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580326880169082881",
      "text": "@janoschjerman @flightradar24 yes and no depends on other traffic, turbulence... they were 25 mins late so going higher = going quicker",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:14:44 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803261993244631e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "581194671902195712",
      "text": "@marcepa49 @flightradar24 @isobelroe and have operated them in sumulators. Also on actual flights when I've been in the flight deck.",
      "timestamp": "Thu Mar 26 20:43:02 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.810756606905754e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580477832826130432",
      "text": "@Minus777 @flightradar24 @isobelroe No, somebody had just initiated the descent, and might have been unconcious or dead just after that.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 21:14:34 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.804773207351337e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580329932577980416",
      "text": "@neilh1983 @Minus777 @london_thfc @flightradar24 @isobelroe Exact! Instead of headingright into the mountains",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:26:52 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.80329566419456e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580330315660558338",
      "text": "@Minus777 @london_thfc @marcepa49 @flightradar24 @isobelroe too early to say but lack of divert suggests something bad happened.",
      "timestamp": "Tue Mar 24 11:28:23 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.803299355516109e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "580476902344941569",
      "text": "@Minus777 @flightradar24 @isobelroe Unless they became rapidly unconcious",
